    { version = "2.4.1", text = "Aura ordering on every aura frame, and the swipe choice back on Buffs & Debuffs.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• |cffffffffAura Ordering|r, a new section right below Auras in Edit Mode on every unit frame with auras: player, target, focus, pet and their targets, party, raid, main tanks and boss frames.\n• Aura Ordering: |cffffffffSort By|r (Default, Order Applied, Time Left or Name), |cffffffffReverse Order|r, and |cffffffffYour Auras First|r (with Time Left or Name). Default keeps Blizzard's order; nothing changes until you pick one. On party, raid and boss frames the buff and debuff rows are sorted; Bigger Boss Debuffs, dispel icons and the big defensive keep their order.\n• Buffs & Debuffs: the same Aura Ordering options in a new section of their settings page (Order Applied by default, as before). The icon shape and timer options now sit under |cffffffffGeneral|r.\n• Buffs & Debuffs: |cffffffffSwipe|r is back in General: Over the icon, Around the border, Both or None.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• The aura swipe now runs over the icon and its border together (|cffffffffBoth|r): the default on Buffs & Debuffs, and on every unit frame aura (player, target, focus, pet, party, raid, main tanks and boss).\n• Buffs & Debuffs, Around the border: a slightly thicker ring and richer border colours." },
    { version = "2.4.0", text = "New aura filters, party and boss frames on Forever Style's frame plate, Growth for party and raid frames, a reworked controller radial, and a full clean-up pass.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Party and boss frames in |cffffffffForever Style|r now sit on the frame plate like the player and target frames, with a |cffffffffScale|r slider. The name box glows for your target and for dispellable debuffs, and the ring flashes on aggro. Forever Style now also uses the ring party and boss frames.\n• Party frames: |cffffffffGrowth|r (Down or Up), right below Style.\n• Raid frames: |cffffffffGrowth|r (From the Middle, Down or Up), right below Sample Raid, for groups in rows. The main tank frames follow it.\n• Party frames: |cffffffffPets|r and |cffffffffParty Targets|r dropdowns (Off, Bottom of the Frame, Right of the Frame) above Spacing. They replace the Show Pets and Show Party Targets checkboxes. Both on the right stack, both at the bottom share a row.\n• |cffffffffHide Buffs|r on the player, party and raid frames (right below Debuffs): hide permanent buffs (the default), or buffs longer than 15, 10, 5 or 1 minutes. Off shows every buff.\n• |cffffffffOnly My Buffs|r on party and raid frames: only the buffs you cast.\n• |cffffffffDispellable Debuffs Only|r on party and raid frames: only the debuffs you can dispel.\n• |cffffffffFocus Boss Debuffs|r on the player, party and raid frames: in a boss fight, only the boss and role debuffs show. Every debuff shows elsewhere.\n• Main tank frames have their own Power Bar Height, aura places, Aura Size and aura filters, in Frame and Auras sections.\n• Raid frames: new inside aura places (Centre, Centre Left, Centre Right); the places drop the \"Inside,\" text.\n• Raid frames: |cffffffffGroup Numbers|r are now \"Group N\" headings above each group. Edit Mode samples follow Sort By and show a sample big defensive.\n• Target and focus frames (FlareUI and Forever Style): |cffffffffHigh Level Skull|r in Icons (on by default). It shows the skull for mobs whose level reads \"??\". Off shows a red \"??\".\n• Pet frame: |cffffffffHappiness Position|r (Centre, Right of the Frame, Left of the Frame) under Pet Happiness.\n• Radial Menu: |cffffffffGame Menu|r and |cffffffffMacros|r in the Panels library.\n• Radial Menu: right-click closes an open radial in Hold activation.\n• Radial Menu, controller: LB and RB switch the aimed button's sub-radial choice. The centre shows the right stick icon in the Gamepad UI.\n• Quest Tracker: now works in the Gamepad UI too.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Radial Menu, controller: |cffffffffL3|r opens the radial, the right stick aims, |cffffffffR3|r uses the button, and B or L3 closes it. The camera holds still while it is open and you can keep walking. R3 is the ping again whenever the radial is closed.\n• Enemy and neutral levels use Blizzard's own difficulty colours (green, yellow, orange, red, grey) on every frame and tooltip, in every style. Friendly levels stay gold.\n• |cffffffffMirror|r on target, focus and boss frames, in FlareUI and Forever Style, only turns the bars' direction now. The portrait and icons keep their places.\n• Party frames: the |cffffffffOrientation|r option is gone; party frames are always vertical.\n• Party and boss frames: auras above or below the frame take one row, so the frames sit closer together.\n• Party, raid and main tank frames: the big defensive is a fixed size (larger on the Forever Style plate). Missing buffs sit centred under it. Every aura sample in Edit Mode has its border.\n• Raid and main tank defaults: new aura places and sizes, height 60, and a main tank position at the bottom left.\n• Party and focus frames show first names only outside Forever Style (Full Player Names still decides elsewhere).\n• Tooltips: the name line shows the name only. One tag at the end of the level line: (Boss) in red, (Elite) and (Rare) in gold; the elite \"+\" is gone. Players read \"Level N Race Class\" in white, and the faction line is coloured (Horde red, Alliance blue).\n• The pet happiness face is a little smaller.\n• A clean-up pass across the whole addon: faster chat lines, damage meter timer, tooltips, quest tracker and nameplate quest tags, plus tidier code.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Radial Menu in the Gamepad UI: opening the bags (or Social) from a radial no longer causes a \"blocked\" error and a long freeze.\n• Hide Tutorials now closes every tutorial tip, not only some.\n• The player's level no longer turns gold after a level-up in the ring styles.\n• Proc Glow no longer leaves a glow stuck after it is switched off and on.\n• Radial Menu: deleting a radial and pressing Undo restores its keybinds too. A slot keeps its highlight when an item finishes loading.\n• Settings: the \"module is off\" card no longer covers search results. The welcome screen counts Resource Bars as a module.\n• Chat and damage meter hooks are no longer added again on every settings change.\n• The weapon enchant tooltip no longer keeps lines from the last unit you hovered." },
    { version = "2.3.1", text = "|cffffd100New|r\n• Tooltips: |cffffffffShow threat|r (on by default, above Show target): turn it off to hide your threat percentage on enemy tooltips." },
    { version = "2.3.0", text = "Radial Menu opening options, chat link tooltips, and more control over how every unit frame looks.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n• Radial Menu: |cffffffffMenu position|r (Options tab): open radials at your mouse cursor (the default) or in the middle of the screen. Radial macros open there too.\n• Radial Menu: |cffffffffActivation|r (Options tab): |cffffffffHold|r (as before: hold the key, point, release) or |cffffffffToggle|r: press the key to open the radial and keep it open. Left-click or press the key again uses the slice you point at, right-click goes back a level or closes, Escape closes. Middle-click a nested radial to open it in place of the current one; the mouse wheel still steps through it.\n• Chat: |cffffffffLink tooltips on hover|r (Tweaks, on by default): point at an item, spell or quest link in chat to see its tooltip, without clicking.\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffBackground Opacity|r at the end of Look in Edit Mode, on every unit frame (player, target, focus, pet, player cast bar, target of target, target of focus, party, raid and boss): how dark the empty part of the bars is, from 0% to 100%. Cast bars follow their frame's setting.\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffFull Player Names|r (Look, on by default): players' first names and surnames on every unit frame. Off shows the first name only.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Unit Frames: |cffffffffBorder Texture|r is now on every frame in FlareUI Style and Addon Style, the player, target and focus frames included. Forever Style has no border options at all: its border is fixed on every frame.\n• Unit Frames: the level of a friendly unit (anything you can't attack) shows in Blizzard's gold, in every style. Enemies keep the difficulty colours.\n• Bar and border dropdowns: FlareUI's own options come first, then a line and the bars or borders other addons add, A-Z. LibSharedMedia's built-in Blizzard bars and borders are no longer listed.\n• FlareUI's options in those dropdowns: FlareUI Thick and FlareUI Thin for Border Texture; None and FlareUI Frames for the Chat, Damage Meter and Quest Tracker borders; FlareUI Flat, FlareUI Forever and FlareUI Striped for Bar, Cast Bar and Absorb Texture. A frame already set to something no longer listed keeps it.\n• |cffffffffFrame Texture|r is gone from Cast Bar Texture and Absorb Texture." },
    { version = "2.2.1", text = "|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Target and focus frames: switching straight from one target to another no longer leaves the last target's debuffs on the frame. They showed up as duplicates, and their timers sat at 0 or were missing (reported in a dungeon). Party, boss and raid frames get the same fix when a new unit takes a frame (a new boss, a roster change).\n• Target and focus frames: |cffffffffOnly My Debuffs|r now shows only the debuffs you cast. Before, it showed every player's debuffs." },
